    [BugFix][Model] Honor BF16 KDA recurrent-state configuration for GLM-5.3-Flash (#18857)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Honor `mamba_ssm_cache_dtype` for GLM KDA recurrent state by passing it
    directly to the upstream `MambaStateDtypeCalculator.kda_state_dtype` in
    both layer allocation and model-level cache sizing. This makes explicit
    BF16 requests take effect consistently and avoids duplicating the
    upstream dtype policy.
    
    Refs #15665.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16` selects BF16 KDA recurrent-state
    storage. `auto` and explicit `float32` retain FP32, and unsupported FP16
    state is rejected. BF16 storage can affect numerical results and
    automatically selected cache geometry.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `tests/ut/models/test_glm5next_kda_state_dtype.py` covers dtype
    selection, model/layer cache-spec consistency, page sizing, and
    rejection of unsupported state dtypes.
    - Existing `tests/ut/models/test_glm5next_kda_contracts.py` coverage
    includes FP32 and BF16 state.
    - Local Ruff lint/format, Python compilation, release-note YAML parsing,
    and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Latest head `201ffbbdd`: [Linux
    pre-commit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39575229458/job/119138985799)
    passed, including mypy for Python 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12.
    - CPU UT passed on both dependencies: [verified vLLM
    main](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39575229458/job/119141388298):
    **11,999 passed, 78 skipped**;
    [v0.31.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39575229458/job/119141388243):
    **11,995 passed, 82 skipped**. The 19 KDA dtype and operator-contract
    cases passed in each matrix.
    - Downstream hardware CI has not completed; the workflow is still
    selecting tests.
    - Full-model BF16 numerical accuracy and NPU execution were not
    revalidated for this review update; CPU interface tests do not establish
    model accuracy.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
